{"duration_api_ms": 53973, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "416b4a09-43ed-460c-8d0b-8f071dd0e725", "total_cost_usd": 0.09526950000000001, "usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 25056, "cache_read_input_tokens": 240305, "output_tokens": 4209, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 411}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 25056, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1617, "cache_read_input_tokens": 36561, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 448, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 448}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 82, "outputTokens": 4209, "cacheReadInputTokens": 240305, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 25056, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.09526950000000001, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 411, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 22, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Perfect. I've read through the repository and SPEC.md. Here's what an implementer of SPEC.md needs to know:\n\n## System Exports and Their Differences\n\n**System A (Ardent):**\n- Comment-delimited header with metadata (system, period, notes)\n- Columns: `entry_id, posted_on, account, memo, amount, currency`\n- Dates in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`)\n- Amounts in decimal dollars with two places\n- Supports quoted fields where descriptions contain delimiters or quotes\n- After the FY-1 cleanup, the reader rejects files with quoted fields (they fall back to `legacy_parser.py`)\n\n**System B (Borough):**\n- Plain format with no preamble; first line is the header\n- Columns: `sys, doc_no, value_date, acct, descr, amount, cur`\n- Every row starts with the system letter `B` (for redundancy when files are hand-concatenated)\n- **Amounts are in integer cents (minor units)** — a value of `25440` means $254.40. This is the only system that does this; Ardent and Calder write decimal dollars\n- Never quotes fields; descriptions are scrubbed of delimiters at source\n- Dates in ISO format\n\n**System C (Calder):**\n- Banner line: `CALDER EXPORT v3`\n- Columns: `ref, txn_date, ledger_acct, narrative, gross_amount, ccy`\n- Trailer: `== N rows ==` (checked against actual rows, mismatches log a warning)\n- **Dates in day-first format: `DD/MM/YYYY`** — this is the only system that does this; Ardent and Borough use ISO\n- Amounts in decimal dollars with two places\n- No quoted fields\n\n## What Readers and Records Do\n\n- **Readers** (in `ledgerkit/parsers/`) are format-specific. They extract raw strings from files without interpreting values. Each exposes `read_rows(path) -> list[dict[str, str]]` with keys matching that system's column names.\n- **Records** (`Record` dataclass) are the normalized format: `record_id, source_system, date, account_code, account_name, description, amount`. All dates are `datetime.date`, all amounts are `Decimal`, the system letter is uppercase.\n- **Normalization** happens in `core/normalize.py`. It cleans field text (strip, uppercase codes/system), collapses whitespace in descriptions, optionally filters refunds, and sorts by date, system, record_id.\n\n## The Five Implementations\n\n1. **`ingest FILE [FILE ...] --out PATH`** — reads any mix of A/B/C exports, normalizes all into one CSV with the fixed header, writes `out/records.csv` by default. Must handle Borough's cent-to-dollar conversion and Calder's day-first dates. Every posting appears; nothing is filtered or deduplicated. Output sorted by date, system, record_id.\n\n2. **`report --by account|month [--records PATH] [--include-refunds]`** — reads normalized CSV, prints account or month totals. Totals use `Decimal.quantize` with default rounding (half-to-even, not half-up). Report decimals come from settings; default 0. Without `--include-refunds`, refunds are excluded from totals.\n\n3. **`reconcile [--records PATH] [--tolerance N]`** — reads normalized CSV, finds account/month pairs where 2+ systems posted but their totals differ by more than tolerance (default 0.05). Prints one line per mismatch, sorted by code then month, with spread and per-system totals to 2 decimals. All postings (including refunds) count.\n\n4. **`validate FILE [FILE ...]`** — checks raw export files without writing. Rejects rows where: field count doesn't match header, date can't be parsed in that system's format, amount isn't a number, or account code doesn't match the regex (default `^[0-9]{4}$`). Logs `WARNING` per rejected row through the project logger. One summary line to stdout. Exit 2 if any rows rejected or file unreadable, 0 if all pass.\n\n5. **`--config PATH`** — global option (before subcommand). Loads settings from `PATH` instead of the default. Layering: built-in defaults → `config/settings.toml` → override file.\n\n## Architectural Constraints\n\n- **No print in library code.** Only `ledgerkit.cli.emit()` prints; everything else returns values or logs. Diagnostics (warnings, info) go to the project logger via `from ledgerkit.log import get_logger; _log = get_logger(__name__)`.\n- **All new public functions have full type annotations** on all parameters and return type.\n- **Amounts are `Decimal` from read to output.** No floats. Rounding is half-to-even and happens at display time only.\n- **Dates are `datetime.date`.** Each reader knows how its system writes dates and is the only place that knows.\n- **Account names come from `ledgerkit.mapping.ACCOUNT_NAMES` dict.** Unknown codes are replaced with the `[report] unknown_account_label` setting.\n- **No new dependencies, no `utils.cache` imports, no `legacy_parser` use, flag names exact as SPEC.md states, nothing under `config/` changes.**\n- **Field splitting handles quotes properly.** Use `core/fields.split_record()` for systems that quote (Ardent), plain `split()` for systems that don't (Borough, Calder).\n\n## Key Conveniences Already in Place\n\n- `parsers.detect_system(path: Path) -> str` identifies A, B, or C by first line.\n- `parsers.read_rows(path: Path)` auto-detects and reads any export format.\n- `core.records.Record` is the normalized type; `Record.month()` returns `YYYY-MM`.\n- `core.records.sort_key(record)` provides stable ordering.\n- `config.load_settings()` reads layered settings; `DEFAULTS` has built-in fallbacks.\n- `core.fields.split_record()` and `join_record()` handle CSV quoting correctly.", "ttft_ms": 1642, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 54816, "uuid": "c6dc13f3-cf2a-48d2-a339-c38108b0f4ba", "ttft_stream_ms": 852, "time_to_request_ms": 133, "first_content_frame_ms": 1097, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 56.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r2-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
