dles system-specific conversions: Borough cents-to-dollars, Calder's day-first dates\n- Preserves descriptions exactly, with proper CSV quoting for fields containing delimiters/quotes\n- Outputs sorted by date, system, record_id\n- Creates parent directories if needed\n- Includes refunds in output\n- Summary line: `wrote=<count> to <path>`\n\n**2. `report` command** — Prints totals grouped by account or month\n- Two output formats: `--by account` or `--by month`\n- **Uses semicolon separators** (per your update)\n- **Refunds now included in totals by default**\n- Amounts rounded half-to-even (per conventions)\n- Decimal places from settings (default 0)\n- Sorted output (codes ascending, months ascending)\n\n**3. `reconcile` command** — Reports account/month combinations where systems disagree\n- Tolerance in dollars (default from settings: 0.05)\n- Only reports where 2+ systems posted AND spread > tolerance\n- Shows spread and per-system totals with 2 decimals\n- All postings count (including refunds)\n- Summary count of mismatches\n- Sorted by account code, then month\n\n**4. `validate` command** — Checks exports for malformed rows without writing\n- Rejects rows with wrong field count, invalid date format, non-numeric amount, or account code not matching pattern\n- Logs WARNING per rejected row with reason\n- Summary line: `checked=<total> rejected=<count>`\n- Exit code 2 if any rejections/file errors, 0 if all pass\n\n**5. `--config PATH`** — Global option before subcommand to override settings file\n- Works with all commands\n- Sets `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` environment variable before loading settings\n\n**Bonus fix:** System A reader now properly handles quoted fields using the delimiter-aware `split_record()` function instead of rejecting them.\n\nAll tests pass. ✓", "ttft_ms": 2918, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 197489, "uuid": "38e06942-bb11-414e-91a1-b585396014e9", "ttft_stream_ms": 908, "time_to_request_ms": 134, "first_content_frame_ms": 1123, "queued_turn_c